    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When you see a snowy "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "owl",
            "ref": "v-owl"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", you’ll know how the bird probably got its name: it is snow-white. "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Males",
            "zh": "雄性"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " are almost all white. "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Females",
            "zh": "雌性"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " have more "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "flecks",
            "zh": "斑点"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "These large owls live mostly in the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Arctic",
            "zh": "北极地区"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Sometimes, they fly south in the fall and winter. Their "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "favourite",
            "ref": "v-favourite"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "prey",
            "zh": "猎物"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "lemming",
            "zh": "旅鼠"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They also "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "hunt",
            "ref": "v-hunt"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " rabbits, birds and fish."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Snowy owls have good "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "eyesight",
            "ref": "v-eyesight"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But they can’t see their prey when it’s under snow or a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "thick",
            "ref": "v-thick"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " layer of plants. To hunt for its prey, the owl relies on its "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "keen",
            "zh": "敏锐的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " hearing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Most owls sleep during the day and hunt at night. But snowy owls are "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "active",
            "ref": "v-active"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " during the day, especially in the summertime. They are usually most active at "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "dawn",
            "zh": "黎明"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "dusk",
            "zh": "黄昏"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Young snowy owls leave the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nest",
            "zh": "巢"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " less than a month after they are born. They can fly well when they’re about a month and a half old. But their parents take care of them for another ten weeks or more."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
